-> Operator precedence: * before +, and before ||, comparison before logic
a = 2 + 3 * 4
assert a = 14

b = 10 - 4 / 2
assert b = 8

-> Comparison returns boolean, can use with logic
c = 3 < 5 and 10 > 2
assert c = true

d = 1 > 2 or 3 < 4
assert d = true

e = 1 > 2 and 3 < 4
assert e = false

-> NOT has highest precedence among logical
f = not false and true
assert f = true
